module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Torsion.Free
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.TorsionFree
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.Module
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Valuation.ValuationRing
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The valuative criterion for the stack of coherent sheaves: the affine chart (Stacks 0DM0)

Stacks 0DM0 says that for `X ⟶ B` proper and of finite presentation the morphism
`Cohstack_{X/B} ⟶ B` satisfies the existence part of the valuative criterion of Stacks 0CLK.
After the base change of the first step of the source's proof the assertion is this: for a
valuation ring `R` with fraction field `K`, an algebraic space `X` proper over `R` and a coherent
`𝒪_{X_K}`-module `F_K` on the generic fibre, there is a finitely presented `𝒪_X`-module `F`,
flat over `R`, whose generic fibre is `F_K`.  The source constructs `F` by writing `j_*F_K`,
for `j : X_K ⟶ X` the (affine) inclusion of the generic fibre, as the directed colimit of its
finite type quasi-coherent submodules `F_i` (Stacks 0829), observing that each `F_i` is torsion
free over `R` and hence flat (Stacks 0539), and taking `i` large enough that
`j^*F_i ⟶ F_K` is onto, which is possible because `F_K` is of finite type.  Finite presentation
of the result is Stacks 0DLR.

This file is that construction on an affine chart.  Let `R` be a valuation ring, `A` an
`R`-algebra — the ring of an affine chart of `X` — and `A_K` the ring of the corresponding chart
of the generic fibre `X_K`, that is, the localization of `A` at the image of the nonzero elements
of `R`; this is `A ⊗_R K` for `K` the fraction field of `R`.  Let `N` be an `A_K`-module, the
module `F_K` on that chart, and read it as an `A`-module, which is what `j_*` does on the chart.
Then

* every nonzero element of `R` acts bijectively on `N`, so `N` is torsion free over `R`, and
  therefore so is each of its `A`-submodules, which are hence all flat over `R` — this is the
  source's "`j_*F_K` is a sheaf of `K`-vector spaces, hence flat over `R`" together with
  Stacks 0539;
* if `N` is of finite type over `A_K`, the `A`-submodule generated by a finite generating family
  is of finite type over `A`, flat over `R`, and has `N` as its localization at the nonzero
  elements of `R` — so its inverse image on the chart of `X_K` is `F_K` on the nose.

## Main results

* `StacksDraft.CoherentGenericFibre.isTorsionFree_of_isLocalization`: the generic fibre is
  torsion free over the valuation ring.
* `StacksDraft.CoherentGenericFibre.flat_of_submodule`: every `A`-submodule of the generic fibre
  is flat over the valuation ring.  This is the source's flatness step, and it is Stacks 0539.
* `StacksDraft.CoherentGenericFibre.exists_submodule_finite_flat_isLocalizedModule`:
  **Stacks 0DM0** on an affine chart over a valuation ring — a module of finite type on the
  chart of the generic fibre is the generic fibre of a module of finite type on the chart which
  is flat over the valuation ring.

## What is and is not proved

Proved: the whole chart-wise content of the source's proof, over an arbitrary `R`-algebra `A`
(no finite presentation and no properness needed) and with the module on the generic fibre
assumed only of finite type rather than coherent.  Nothing is assumed about the module that is
to be produced; it is constructed, and the identification of its generic fibre with the
prescribed module is `IsLocalizedModule`, which is the statement that the inverse image of the
constructed module along the chart of `j` is the prescribed module.

Not proved, and therefore not claimed by the tag:

* the first step of the source's proof, the reduction of the statement about
  `Cohstack_{X/B} ⟶ B` to the statement over a valuation ring by base change;
* the gluing of the chart-wise extensions to a module on all of `X`, for which the source uses
  that `j` is affine, so that `j_*F_K` is quasi-coherent, and the colimit presentation of
  Stacks 0829 on `X` itself;
* the properness over `R` of the support of the extension;
* the finite presentation of the extension, for which the source cites Stacks 0DLR;
* consequently also the statement for the 1-morphism `Cohstack_{X/B} ⟶ B` in the sense of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.ValuativeCriterion.Existence` (Stacks 0CLK).  That criterion is
  stated for a 1-morphism of `AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicStacks`, and `Cohstack_{X/B}` is not
  an object of that type in this development: Stacks 08KB is formalised in
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/CoherentStack.lean` as the objects
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.CoherentObject` and the morphisms
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.CoherentHom` together with the *specification*
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.CoherentCategoryData` of a category structure on them, of which no
  value is constructed, and the algebraicity of the resulting stack, Stacks 09DS, is not in this
  development either.

## Implementation notes

The chart of the generic fibre is taken as an arbitrary model `A_K` of the localization of `A`
at `Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid A R⁰`, in the same style as the models of localizations
elsewhere in this development, rather than as `A ⊗_R K` or as a chosen localization; the
fraction field `K` then never has to be mentioned, because the nonzero elements of `R` are
already units in `A_K`.  The `R`-action on `N` is the restriction of the `A`-action, and the
`A`-action is the restriction of the `A_K`-action, which is the chart-level reading of `j_*`.

The generic fibre of the constructed submodule `M` is identified with `N` by
`IsLocalizedModule R⁰ (LinearMap.restrictScalars R M.subtype)`.  Of its three conditions, the
invertibility of the nonzero elements of `R` on `N` is `bijective_smul` and is read off
`IsLocalization.map_units` through the two scalar towers; the surjectivity is the
denominator-clearing of `exists_smul_mem_span`, proved by induction over the `A_K`-span of the
generating family, whose scalar case is `exists_smul_smul_mem`; and the third condition is
trivial because `M.subtype` is injective.

`StacksDraft.GenericFibre.flat_of_isTorsionFree`, the form of Stacks 0539 used here, is already
proved in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Quot/QuotValuativeAffineChart.lean`, the companion
chart-wise statement for the Quot functor (Stacks 0DM4).  It is repeated here as a private
declaration only because that file is not present in the checkout this one was written against;
when the two are in one tree the import should replace the copy.

